:"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":13531659,"digest":"sha256:a23142f12b59444138b588a8a764666b025552a14036f62d83af022153f1a0a5","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-22T19:16:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T19:16:13Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/DocumentDrivenDX/weft/releases/download/v0.4.51/weft_sql-0.4.51-cp39-abi3-manylinux_2_17_x86_64.manylinux2014_x86_64.whl"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DocumentDrivenDX/weft/tarball/v0.4.51","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DocumentDrivenDX/weft/zipball/v0.4.51","body":"\n# Weft 0.4.51\n\n## Release scope\n\nPython wheel candidate for Truss0.0.48 embedders, intended for GitHub release\nassets; the repository maintainer owns publication. The current compiler/build\nsource freeze is `557153731e9f5d0583193a1189a07c6ed485d3d3` (source F), selected\nfrom the public0.4.49 lineage. Full selected-source workspace tests at\n`56d5507c6b0169574277661dd85d8c5feb22e6a7` passed with 1,046 default-profile\ntests and 1,047 qualified-profile tests across 62 summaries per run. No\nprotected compiler/build inputs differ from source F.\n\nThe Mac ARM64 source-F wheel and native module were rebuilt and independently\nchecked. The new module passed 51 exact-feature runtime library tests, 33 native\nentity-selection cases and 5 native facts cases. No new source-F Chromium run is\nclaimed here. Linux packaging and independent archive verification passed for x86_64 and\naarch64 from source F; packaging alone is claimed for both Linux targets. No\nsource-F Linux Truss host or database execution is claimed. Hosted final conformance run 39822650250 completed\nsuccessfully with all source jobs and steps passing. Its testability/workflow identities and limited host-evidence scope are\nrecorded separately. Source-F Truss host gates passed on local macOS\nARM64/PostgreSQL18.6 for 80 migration cases, 62 independent archive cases, six\ncohort tests, 14 policy executions over 10 distinct controls and the\n1,000-object/1,000-edge workload. Four policy executions repeat imported query tests. Publication and\nrelease/tag gates remain separate.\n\n## Audience and channels\n\nTruss and Arras maintainers receive the compiler wheels, SHA256SUMS and exact\nrelease pins through the GitHub release. Applications consume the matching Truss\nhost; the compiler itself does not connect to a database.\n\n## Highlights\n\n- Explicit entity descriptors preserve ordered Fields, related projections and\n  selected native facts; eight facts are available through the declared interface.\n- Truss query ABI1.2 supports bounded indexed sources and eligible key pages,\n  with complete bounded fallback for other admitted queries.\n- Original arras.view0.1.0 Record/Field metadata is admitted only under its exact\n  owning-document vocabulary declaration. Unsupported selected versions refuse.\n\n## Changes and fixes\n\nCompile/IR0.2.8 and backend43/44 are explicit registrations; published0.2.7 behavior\nremains unchanged. Typed resolution diagnostics preserve failure classification.\nThe historical 31 entity compilation cases remain, with two additional Arras\npositive/refusal cases. Separate facts compilation retains five parity cases.\nOpaque Arras metadata does not grant it security or storage semantics.\n\nPublisher receipts bind actual build checkouts, wheel/module hashes and frozen\ncompiler/build/contract inputs. A mixed-source platform cohort refuses publication.\n\n## Breaking changes and required actions\n\nInstall the checksum-verified platform Weft0.4.51 wheel with the matching\nTruss0.0.48 host before selecting the new ABI. Keep exact native module and host\npins aligned; same-version candidate wheels can contain different compiler bytes.\nApplications using the unchanged published ABI need no query-language rewrite.\n\n## Migration or rollback guidance\n\nWeft changes no database schema. Truss owns explicit offline database migration\nand its latest-only runtime policy. Quiesce writers, retain backups and use the\nTruss migration guide before resuming application work. Hold on compiler/host\nmismatch or failed admission; restoring an old application package is not a\nrollback for an upgraded database.\n\n## Known issues and support\n\nThe [source-F evidence packet](../evidence/release051-source557-20261022/README.md)\nrecords the selected workspace results, new Mac wheel/module checks, Linux\npackaging, hosted final conformance and exact installed-Truss host receipts. The\nactive `local-macos-0.4.51.json` records source-F results; the exact prior source-86\nJSON is retained separately as superseded history. Local Truss qualification passed 80 lineage cases, 62 independent cases, six\ncohort/asset-cache tests, 14 policy executions across 10 distinct controls, and\nthe 1,000-object/1,000-edge workload. Four policy executions repeat imported\nquery tests. The successful hosted fresh-host receipt is limited to 2,181 retired\nUMF 0.7 refusals and stated parity controls; it does not qualify current Truss compilation\nor database execution. The Truss host receipts are local macOS/PostgreSQL\nevidence only. The Linux aarch64 wheel has packaging evidence only.\nTable-operation evidence records candidate SQL behavior and binding cases; it\ndoes not qualify generated/runtime operation admission. Managed UC/Spark4.2,\nprotected migration and broad p95 targets are not qualified.\nThe selected release excludes main's separate managed candidates. Arras owns its\nfull adapter acceptance against the public dependency pair.\n\n## References\n\n- [Exact selected-source evidence](../evidence/truss-selective-sources-20261022/arras-source86c/receipt.json)\n- [Source-F 0.4.51 rebuild, packaging and hosted conformance evidence](../evidence/release051-source557-20261022/README.md)\n- [Historical 0.4.51 packaging and scoped Linux evidence](../evidence/release051-final-packet-20261022/README.md)\n- [Application read contract](../../02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-004-application-reads.md)\n- [Support and issues](https://github.com/DocumentDrivenDX/weft/issues)\n"}